ecord ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2657,CALCIUM,\"Calcium is an essential mineral that plays a crucial role in maintaining bone health and is vital for the development of strong bones and teeth, particularly in children and preterm infants. Its importance extends to various age groups, with specific intake recommendations outlined in dietary guidelines. Calcium is also significant in the context of osteoporosis management, as it is often supplemented to aid in bone density recovery, especially in patients with conditions such as Anorexia Nervosa or those undergoing dialysis, where a daily intake of 1-1.5 g is recommended.\n\nIn addition to its role in bone health, calcium is involved in several biological processes, including the regulation of homeostasis in the body and the signaling process that triggers insulin secretion from β-cells. Research has explored the relationship between calcium intake and cancer risk, as well as its potential inverse relationship with blood pressure, particularly in individuals sensitive to salt.\n\nHowever, calcium's metabolism can be affected by various factors, such as gastric resection, which may decrease its absorption and lead to secondary hyperparathyroidism and increased bone resorption. Furthermore, while calcium is vital for health, excessive intake can contribute to the formation of kidney stones, particularly calcium oxalate stones, and its excretion is influenced by dietary factors.\n\nCalcium is predominantly found in dairy products and leafy greens, making it an important nutrient in diets aimed at preventing osteoporosis and promoting overall cardiovascular function. Overall, calcium is a vital micronutrient that supports numerous physiological functions and is essential for maintaining optimal health.\",24\r\n5338,METABOLIC SYNDROME,\"Metabolic syndrome is a cluster of conditions that significantly increase the risk of heart disease, stroke, and diabetes. This syndrome is often associated with various factors, including dietary habits, obesity, and insulin resistance. It is particularly prevalent in certain populations, such as patients with Klinefelter syndrome and individuals who have undergone liver transplantation. Management of metabolic syndrome can be achieved through dietary changes, with the Mediterranean diet being one effective approach. Overall, metabolic syndrome represents a serious health concern that requires attention to lifestyle and dietary factors to mitigate its associated risks.\",10\r\n5553,PREGNANCY,\"Pregnancy is a physiological condition characterized by various metabolic adaptations in the mother that are essential for supporting fetal development. It necessitates careful nutritional management, particularly for women with diabetes, to ensure both proper fetal growth and the health of the mother.\",2\r\n5207,POTASSIUM,\"Potassium is an essential mineral and electrolyte that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is commonly measured in blood tests to assess adrenal function and other health conditions. Found abundantly in fruits, vegetables, and other foods, potassium is vital for heart health and may aid in controlling blood pressure, particularly in individuals with high sodium intake. \n\nIn addition to its cardiovascular benefits, potassium influences kidney health and the formation of kidney stones. It helps regulate fluid balance in the body, making it important for overall health. However, potassium intake may need to be restricted in the diets of certain patients, especially those with chronic kidney disease, to prevent complications such as hyperkalemia. For patients without diuresis undergoing treatment with ACE inhibitors, potassium intake should not exceed 1 mEq/kg/day. Consequently, potassium levels are closely monitored and managed in dietary recommendations for individuals with kidney issues to ensure their health and well-being.\",13\r\n2654,PHOSPHORUS,\"Phosphorus is a vital mineral that plays a critical role in bone health and energy production. It is particularly important for various age groups, with specific dietary reference intake levels outlined in dietary guidelines. The mineral is essential for maintaining calcium homeostasis and is often studied in relation to chronic kidney disease (CKD) and dietary management.\n\nIn the context of dietary intake, phosphorus is significant for premature infants, as it supports their bone health and overall development. However, for patients with chronic kidney disease, phosphorus intake must be carefully managed. High levels of phosphorus can lead to nutritional deficits and bone disease, necessitating dietary restrictions to prevent complications. For individuals undergoing dialysis, the recommended phosphorus intake is approximately 17 mg/kg/day.\n\nOverall, phosphorus is a crucial dietary mineral that must be balanced to support health, particularly in vulnerable populations such as infants and patients with renal insufficiency.\",12\r\n2655,VITAMIN D,\"Vitamin D is a crucial fat-soluble vitamin that plays a significant role in maintaining bone health and muscle function. It is essential for calcium absorption, which is vital for bone integrity, and has been linked to various health outcomes, including the risk of cancer, cardiovascular disease, and frailty. Vitamin D deficiency is a common concern, particularly in specific populations such as patients with anorexia nervosa, liver disease, and those who have undergone bariatric surgery, as well as in older adults and preterm infants. \n\nResearch indicates that optimizing Vitamin D levels is important for preventing metabolic bone disease and supporting overall health. It is often recommended for supplementation in individuals at risk of osteoporosis and is particularly relevant for maintaining muscle health in older adults, potentially aiding in the treatment of sarcopenia. Additionally, Vitamin D deficiency has been associated with the development of food allergies and is common in patients with conditions like EPOC and BQ.\n\nDosage recommendations for Vitamin D are typically based on individual factors such as calcium, phosphorus, and parathyroid hormone (PTH) levels, with a general guideline to maintain 25OH-vitamin D levels above 30 ng/dl. The importance of adequate Vitamin D intake is emphasized across various health contexts, including its role in immune function and fall prevention in older adults. Overall, Vitamin D is recognized as a vital nutrient that supports bone health and has implications for a wide range of health outcomes.\",27\r\n3121,CHRONIC KIDNEY DISEASE,\"Chronic kidney disease (CKD) is a long-term condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to function effectively, which can significantly impact overall health and bodily functions. This condition often necessitates dietary management, particularly concerning phosphorus and calcium, as imbalances in these minerals can adversely affect bone health. Additionally, CKD is associated with muscle wasting and is frequently linked to sarcopenia, especially in older populations. The effects of chronic kidney disease can lead to frailty in the elderly, further complicating their health status and quality of life. Nutritional support and careful management are essential components in addressing the challenges posed by this condition.\",7\r\n11984,KIDNEY STONES,Kidney stones are solid masses made of crystals that originate in the kidneys. They can cause significant pain and complications for those affected.,9\r\n8429,NUTRITIONAL CONTROL,\"Nutritional control for patients undergoing bariatric surgery aims to ensure adequate intake, limit complications, and address nutritional deficits.\",10\r\n10085,DIALYSIS PERITONEAL,\"DIALYSIS PERITONEAL refers to peritoneal dialysis, a treatment for kidney failure that utilizes the lining of the abdomen to filter waste from the blood. This method effectively removes toxins and excess fluids, providing an alternative to traditional hemodialysis for patients with compromised kidney function.\",15\r\n7546,BREAST CANCER,\"Breast cancer is a type of cancer that develops from breast tissue. It is a significant area of study, particularly concerning its risk factors, which include various dietary intakes. Numerous studies have been conducted to examine the relationship between dietary factors and the risk of developing breast cancer, highlighting the importance of nutrition in understanding this disease.\",4\r\n7746,COLON CANCER,\"Colon cancer is a type of cancer that affects the colon and is a significant focus of medical research, particularly in relation to dietary factors.\",3\r\n5692,HYPOCALCEMIA,\"Hypocalcemia is a medical condition characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood. This condition can arise from various factors, including vitamin D deficiency. Additionally, hypocalcemia is commonly observed in a significant percentage of patients suffering from pancreatitis, where it is often associated with metabolic disturbances.\",3\r\n5696,ANTIEPILEPTIC MEDICATION,\"Antiepileptic medications can affect the metabolism of vitamin D, potentially leading to deficiencies in patients taking these drugs.\",1\r\n5695,MALABSORPTION,\"Malabsorption is a medical condition characterized by the intestine's inability to properly absorb nutrients from the gastrointestinal tract. This condition is often observed in patients with celiac disease and can result in various nutritional deficiencies, including vitamin D deficiency.\",1\r\n5697,TUBERCULOSTATIC MEDICATION,\"Tuberculostatic medications are used to treat tuberculosis and can also impact vitamin D metabolism, contributing to deficiency.\",1\r\n10861,FRUITS AND VEGETABLES,\"Fruits and vegetables are recommended for their high content of vitamins, minerals, and antioxidants that promote heart health.\",3\r\n11986,OXALATE,\"Oxalate is a compound commonly found in a variety of foods. It has the potential to combine with calcium, which can lead to the formation of kidney stones. Additionally, the levels of oxalate in urine can be influenced by dietary choices, further contributing to the risk of kidney stone development.\",2\r\n11558,ADDITIVES,\"Substances added to processed foods that can increase phosphorus intake, impacting patients with chronic kidney disease.\",1\r\n11557,DIETARY RESTRICTION,The practice of limiting certain foods to manage phosphorus levels in patients with chronic kidney disease.,1\r\n9163,BURCELIN R,Burcelin R is a researcher who has investigated the interactions between the immune system and microbiota in the context of metabolic diseases. His work focuses on understanding the cross-talk between these two systems and how it influences metabolic health.,1\r\n7737,WORLD JOURNAL OF DIABETES,\"A journal that discusses the role of various factors, including vitamin D, in diabetes and metabolic syndrome.\",1\r\n11988,RENAL ANATOMY,,1\r\n11985,URIC ACID,\"Uric acid is a waste product formed from the breakdown of purines, and its levels are significant in the formation of certain types of kidney stones.\",1\r\n11987,PHOSPHATE,Phosphate is a chemical compound that can also contribute to the formation of kidney stones.,1\r\n7745,DAIRY,\"Dairy products are food items derived from milk, which are often studied for their nutritional value and potential health impacts, including cancer risk.\",1\r\n5693,HYPOPARATHYROIDISM,\"Hypoparathyroidism is a medical condition characterized by insufficient production of parathyroid hormone by the parathyroid glands. This deficiency results in low levels of calcium in the blood, which can lead to various complications, including potential bone issues. Patients with hypoparathyroidism often require treatment with vitamin D to help manage their calcium levels ef